---
import { getEntry } from "astro:content";
import BaseHead from "../base/BaseHead.astro";
import MobileLayout from "../base/layouts/MobileLayout.astro";
import MailCTA from "../components/MailCTA.astro";

export const prerender = true;

const v247 = await getEntry("sloks", "2/47");
const v135 = await getEntry("sloks", "1/35");
---

<BaseHead
  title="Daily Bhagavad Gita Email — One Verse Every Morning | Geeta.Prasuco.com"
  description="A free daily Bhagavad Gita email subscription: one short, practical teaching in your inbox every morning, explained in simple words and connected to real-life problems. No spam, unsubscribe anytime."
>
  <MobileLayout>
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-8 space-y-10">
      <header class="space-y-4">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-orange-600 uppercase tracking-wider">
          Geeta in Mail · Free daily email
        </p>
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 font-serif leading-tight">
          A Daily Bhagavad Gita Email, Written for a Modern Morning
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
          One verse. One short, practical teaching. In your inbox every morning.
          A daily Gita email subscription for people who want more clarity and
          less chaos — without reading a book cover to cover.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 font-serif">
          What you get, every morning
        </h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 bg-orange-50/40 rounded-2xl">
            <span class="text-orange-600 font-bold mt-0.5">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong>One verse in Sanskrit and English</strong>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5">
                The original verse with a faithful, plain-English translation.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 bg-orange-50/40 rounded-2xl">
            <span class="text-orange-600 font-bold mt-0.5">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong>A 1-minute teaching</strong>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5">
                The verse unpacked simply and tied to a real-life problem —
                stress, decision-making, confusion, duty.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 bg-orange-50/40 rounded-2xl">
            <span class="text-orange-600 font-bold mt-0.5">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong>No clutter, no spam</strong>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5">
                A short read that fits your morning, not another marketing
                newsletter. Unsubscribe anytime.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 font-serif">
          A taste of what arrives each day
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
          Here is the style of the daily teaching — the most quoted verse in
          the Gita, on doing your duty without clinging to the result:
        </p>
        <blockquote class="bg-orange-50/40 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-3">
          <p class="text-2xl md:text-3xl leading-relaxed font-medium text-sanskrit">
            {v247?.data.text.replaceAll("\n", " ")}
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm italic text-gray-500 leading-loose">
            {v247?.data.transliteration.replaceAll("\n", " ")}
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            "You have a right to your actions, but never to the fruits of your
            actions. Don't let results be your motive, and don't be attached to
            inaction."
          </p>
          <a
            href="/2/47/"
            class="inline-block text-sm font-medium text-orange-600 hover:underline"
          >
            Read the full verse with word meanings →
          </a>
        </blockquote>
        <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
          In your inbox this becomes a few sentences: do the work in front of
          you with full effort, let go of the outcome, and you free yourself
          from anxiety. That's the whole teaching, delivered daily.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 font-serif">
          Why a daily email, not another app
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
          Apps compete for your attention. Email meets you where you already
          are. A daily verse works because it's:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
          <li>
            · <strong>Consistent</strong> — the same short habit every morning
            builds momentum over weeks.
          </li>
          <li>
            · <strong>Practical</strong> — each teaching is connected to an
            everyday problem, not abstract philosophy.
          </li>
          <li>
            · <strong>Deep, slowly</strong> — the Gita is meant to be digested
            one verse at a time, not skimmed in an evening.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
          When a verse resonates, you can open it on Geeta Mini and explore the
          original Sanskrit, word-by-word meanings, and multiple commentaries:
          <a href="/2/47/" class="text-orange-600 hover:underline">2.47</a>,{" "}
          <a href="/6/35/" class="text-orange-600 hover:underline">6.35</a>,{" "}
          <a href="/12/6/" class="text-orange-600 hover:underline">12.6</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 font-serif">
          How the subscription works
        </h2>
        <ol class="space-y-3 list-decimal list-inside text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
          <li>
            Enter your email on the{" "}
            <a href="/geeta-mail/" class="text-orange-600 hover:underline">
              Geeta in Mail page
            </a>
            .
          </li>
          <li>
            Confirm your subscription (double opt-in, so your inbox stays clean).
          </li>
          <li>
            Receive one teaching every morning. Read it in a minute, carry it
            through the day.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
          It's free, built by a small independent project, and you can leave at
          any time with one click.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="pt-4">
        <MailCTA />
      </div>
    </article>
  </MobileLayout>
</BaseHead>
